From: Max More <more@chaph.usc.edu>
Date: Thu, 11 Aug 1994 23:51:48 -0700 (PDT)
Subject: [#94-8-126] EC: Cut it out!

I remember when "EC' was just a joke.

Quite frequently I've been seeing extropians talking of things as EC or 
not EC, with no detectable sign that they are doing so humorously.  
Originally "EC" was invented as a playful jab at "PC" -- Politically 
Correct.  If the "liberal" dogmatists can label ideas, conclusions, and 
people as PC, let's poke fun by labeling things EC -- Extropically 
Correct!

PLEASE, if you're going to use the term EC, make it clear that you're 
doing so humorously.  Otherwise we're going to encounter people who 
say "Oh, yes, those Extropians.  They think that there's only one correct 
way to do anything, one correct technological approach, one correct way 
to live..."

Unfortunately, "Extropically Reasonable" or "Extropically Defensible" 
aren't as memetically infectious, even though they are more in the spirit 
of extropian thought and action.

Onward!

